independence square was a rallying point  for young sri lankans on monday and  rally they did  all echoing a common theme  enough is enough  the president and his government must  resign people were afraid earlier but  now i think it's time that we make a  stand and that we stand up for our  rights because this is our sri lanka and  our future protesters had planned a  major show of strength on sunday here at  this monument in colombo built to  celebrate sri lanka's independence from  britain in 1948  but instead their current leaders  imposed a curfew banned any public  gathering and barricaded all roads that  led to independence square  on monday university students added  their voice to the protests we are doing  what we can we are standing we are  standing our ground and we are staying  here to say no you have to go we need a  better country now we are not going to  give in we are not going to be pacified  by this you know minor changes we want  tangible real tangible change we want to  see  everybody step down students from pera  denier university also stepped out a day  earlier refusing to back down when  confronted by police  they fought with police despite a curfew  imposed to limit the unrest  after hours of tense standoff police  used tear gas and water cannon to  disperse  them anger and frustration has mounted  against president gotabe rajapaksa and  his government after the cost of living  skyrocketed and essential items became  scarce  many sri lankans blame what they say is  the administration's mismanagement lack  of planning and corruption for  aggravating economic difficulties sri  lanka shares with many countries around  the world  the government's attempt to restrict  movement through a state of emergency  and a curfew have failed to stop the  protests  the entire cabinet has resigned  allowing the president and his brother  the prime minister to appoint a new  temporary cabinet  the president has now sworn in a  temporary cabinet of four ministers but  protesters say they are not fooled by  such actions  sri lanka is facing multiple crises  there's little or no foreign currency to  buy basic essentials like food medicine  gas and fuel  and now political uncertainty but sri  lankans are taking a stand  miner fernandez al jazeera colombo
 

